The Sharpe Ratio is calculated as the excess return over the risk‑free rate divided by the portfolio’s standard deviation:

\[
\text{Sharpe} = \frac{\text{Return}_{\text{market}} - \text{RiskFree}}{\sigma}
= \frac{10\% - 5\%}{15\%}
= \frac{5\%}{15\%}
= \frac{1}{3}
\approx 0.33
\]

So the market Sharpe Ratio is approximately **0.33**.

